  "register": "notes",
  "source_dataset": "MIMIC_IV_NOTE",
  "text": "Allergies:\ntree nuts\n\nChief Complaint:\nelective admission for chemo\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nPer admitting physician:\n\n___ is a ___ yo woman with hx of L thigh melanoma in \nsitu\ns/p resection, R mandible lentigo maligna awaiting ___, newly\ndiagnosed CNS lymphoma, here for C3 of HD-MTX. \n\nShe was discharged ___ after receiving port placement and C2\nHD-MTX. She had MTX-related transaminitis (ALT 200s, AST 100s)\nand new cerebral edema w/ 3 mm midline shift. \n\nFor her cerebral edema: She reported worsening headache ___ and\nCTH revealed 3 mm leftward midline shift. MRI showed tumor\nregression, but significant increase in vasogenic edema w/\nrepeated evidence of midline shift. She was started on high dose\nsteroids initially, but after discussion with her\nneuro-oncologist, she was transitioned to 4 mg dex daily. \n\nShe was also seen by ophthalmology that admission, who noted \nleft\nvitreal inflammation probably c/w lymphoma. She was started on\nprednisolone drops with plan to re-evaluate this admission for\npossible intravitreal injections.\n\nShe reports today she feels great. She has not had a headache\nsince discharge. Denies blurry vision, double vision. No nausea,\nvomiting. No abdominal discomfort, diarrhea, constipation, chest\npain, sob, cough, cold symptoms, dysuria. \n\nShe started taking sodium bicarb tabs on ___. \n\nAll other review of systems are negative unless stated otherwise\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\n___ w/ CNS lymphoma here for C3 of HD-MTX induction therapy. \n\n# R frontal lobe CNS Lymphoma\n# Concern for ocular lymphoma\nPresented with seizures (lip twitching, left facial droop) \n___. Tolerated prior induction w/ mild transaminitis and \ncerebral edema of unclear etiology in light of concurrent tumor \nregression. She also had L eye vision loss for which she is \nbeing worked up for ocular lymphoma. She was started on \nprednisolone drops. She tolerated this round well with minimal \nnausea and transaminitis.  \n- cont keppra 2 g BID\n- Ophtho saw her inpatient, tapering off her steroid drops w/ \nclose monitoring \n- Return in 2 wks for next tmt\n- tapering off dex by 1 mg \n\n# Cerebral edema, unclear etiology \nDuring C2, developed right sided HA w/ MRI/CT showing new 3 mm \nleftward midline shift despite tumor regression. Initially on \nhigh dose steroids, but decreased to 4 mg dex daily after \ndiscussion with Dr ___. She tolerated 3 mg well. Will \ncontinue to taper by 1 mg q 3 days, then 0.5 mg x 3 days and \nthen stop. \n- Dexamethasone 3 mg daily starting on ___, then 2 mg x 3 days, \n1 mg x 3 days, then 0.5 mg x 3 days \n\n# R mandible lentigo maligna- follows derm here with plan for \neventual slow Mohs. Scheduled ___\n\nBILLING: >30 min spent coordinating care for discharge\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nCNS Lymphoma\nDiffuse maculopathy left eye",
